hasattr() in Python

👉 Checks if an object has a property or method.

Syntax:

hasattr(object, "attribute_name")


✅ Returns True if it exists
❌ Returns False if not

Example:

class Car:
    def __init__(self):
        self.color = "Red"

    def drive(self):
        print("Vroom!")

my_car = Car()

print(hasattr(my_car, "color"))  # True
print(hasattr(my_car, "speed"))  # False
print(hasattr(my_car, "drive"))  # True


💡 Think of it like asking:
"Does this object have this thing?"














