__var__ is for magic methods that Python uses automatically, like __init__; think of it like a birth certificate that’s made for you.
_var means “please treat this as private”, like a diary with a small lock — not truly hidden, but asking for privacy.
__var starts with two underscores (but no ending ones) — Python secretly renames it to protect it, like hiding something in a labeled secret envelope.
var_ adds an underscore at the end to avoid using a reserved word, like naming a dog “Stop_” so it doesn’t confuse the command “Stop.”
